2026-11-06T03:18:56.1348133Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1358013Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1358635Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1359087Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1359324Z 
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1359682Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1359860Z 
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1359982Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360239Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360374Z 
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360439Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360610Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360719Z 
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1360886Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1361209Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:18:56.1361347Z 
